<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leszek the Black</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1241–<a href="/years/1288">1288</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Leszek II the Black</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leszek the Black was a Piast duke who received Sieradz on the division of his father Casimir I's lands in 1267. In 1279 he inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> and Sandomierz and became High Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. He fought off Lithuanian and Mongol raids and a rebellion of nobles, but died childless in 1288, prolonging the fragmentation of Poland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leszek-the-black.jpg" alt="Leszek the Black" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Zuber at Polish Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piecz%C4%99%C4%87_Leszka_Czarnego.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
